// CROWN — latency rides a HOF parameter called inside a TEE body whose
// handler absorbs an UNRELATED effect: `g(f) = f(1) ~> quiet`, handed a
// closure performing E under `with !E`. Expect E_EffectMismatch.
//
// Checked clean through the pinned boot (measured 2026-09-23): the tee
// body's frame exits and settles the parameter's call cell, so `quiet`,
// which absorbs only F, launders E as well.
effect E { op() -> Int }
effect F { other() -> Int }
handler quiet { other() => resume(0) }
fn g(f) = f(1) ~> quiet
fn clean() with !E = g({ x => op() })
fn main() = 0
